event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":120,"item_id":"rs_06f956ce0356d24a016ac947526d348196ac1b5147c4858bc9","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering UI tests**\n\nI'm thinking about adding UI tests using a built-in fake DOM. It seems straightforward — around 130 lines to establish selection boundaries, title errors, and so on. I want to maintain quality without any external dependencies. Since I won't have a browser available, I find a command with Chromium optional but not necessary. The fake DOM will be explicitly used, not for actual acceptance. I'll import tasks without a global document until the call patch restores it. I need minimal class implementation and wait for async listeners to be dispatched by Promise.all, with unit tests for tasks that cover most useful behavior."}

